title: They Are They Which Testify of Me – Christ in the Old Testament
description: Christ in the Old Testament: the promise from the garden, the pictures of Christ in the patriarchs, the tabernacle and the sacrifices, the feasts fulfilled, Christ our King and High Priest, and Christ and His bride, from the teachings on Christ in the Old Testament.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-christ-ot.html
highlight: Christ; lamb

# One deck for the doctrine "Christ in the Old Testament" (158 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- They Are They Which Testify of Me [title]
overline: Doctrine · Christ in the Old Testament
heading: They Testify of Me
sub: Types, shadows and prophecies fulfilled in Christ.
refs: John 5:39; Luke 24:27; Acts 10:43; Hebrews 10:1; Revelation 13:8
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 16871, 15909
--- It is entirely about Him
big: Luke 24:27 | mark: he expounded unto them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself
p: Many argue that Jesus wasn't known in the Old Testament, that salvation by faith didn't exist. There is no anachronism when we see Christ in the Old Testament. It is entirely about Him. He is the Lamb slain before the foundation of the world ([[Revelation 13:8]]).
p: Moses and the prophets all gave witness to His coming. And though they saw it afar off, most dying in faith having not seen Him, but persuaded of Him, many waited, watching for Him ([[Hebrews 11:13]]).
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~16871 | Seeing Christ in Job is no anachronism

=== Christ foretold
# from 6501, 6519, 8055
--- The seed of the woman
kicker: Christ foretold
big: Genesis 3:15 | mark: it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel
p: God the Father who loves man offers the first promise of Christ, while laying out the consequences of bringing sin into the world. The seed who bruises Satan's head, and whom Satan bruises the heel, is Christ. And He covered them with coats of skins ([[Genesis 3:21]]).
p: Revelation 12 is the fulfilment: the woman bringing forth the man child who will crush Satan's head, the dragon seeking to devour Him as soon as He was born ([[Revelation 12:4-5]]). The seed of Satan are his spawn, reprobates. Sons of Belial. Vipers.

# from 7116, 9803, 15082, 17685
--- God will provide himself a lamb
kicker: Christ foretold
big: Genesis 22:8 | mark: God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering
p: Take thine only son to the land of Moriah, which is where Jerusalem is ([[2 Chronicles 3:1]]), for a burnt offering. On the third day Abraham lifted up his eyes. The wood, carried up the mount. The thicket of thorns on the ram, offered in place of the son by God.
p: Jerusalem is where God chose to place His name. Where His name would be killed for our transgressions. God did not require the sacrifice of man, but gave His only begotten Son. Jehovahjireh ([[Genesis 22:14]]).

# from 13093, 14946, 9070, 12030
--- A Prophet like Moses, a Son of David
kicker: Christ foretold
big: Deuteronomy 18:15 | mark: The LORD thy God will raise up unto thee a Prophet from the midst of thee, of thy brethren, like unto me
p: God tells David, through Nathan, that his son will build the house, and the son of David will rule forever. This is a clear picture of Christ ([[1 Chronicles 17:11-14]]).
p: To the secular, this places Jesus in line to be an earthly king. To those called by the Spirit, He is the savior of their souls and heir to the Heavenly Kingdom. The Son of David, and the Son of God ([[Luke 3:38]]).

# from 17751, 17753, 17432
--- Psalm 22 and the cross
kicker: Christ foretold
big: Psalms 22:16-18 | mark: they pierced my hands and my feet; They part my garments among them, and cast lots upon my vesture
p: In the 9th hour, Jesus cried out from the cross the opening line of a song penned by David centuries earlier ([[Matthew 27:46]]). Compassed about by dogs, the Roman soldiers doing the work of the Jews, piercing Jesus' hands and feet. Splayed out upon the cross, His joints distended.
p: *As a sheep before her shearers is dumb, so he openeth not his mouth* ([[Isaiah 53:7]]). Pilate could be excused for not knowing the prophecy. Herod, King of the Jews, and the priests and scribes should have.

# from 15371, 16563, 16617, 16639
--- Bethlehem, the ass, thirty pieces of silver
kicker: Christ foretold
table: The prophecy | Fulfilled in Christ
tr: [[Micah 5:2]] | Born in Bethlehem, whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting
tr: [[Hosea 11:1]] | Out of Egypt have I called my son
tr: [[Zechariah 9:9]] | Thy King cometh, lowly, and riding upon an ass
tr: [[Zechariah 11:12-13]] | Thirty pieces of silver cast to the potter
tr: [[Zechariah 13:6-7]] | The wounds in His hands; smite the shepherd
tr: [[Daniel 9:25-26]] | The seventy weeks: Messiah cut off
p: Micah 5 hardly needs any commentary, it is so clear. God dropped a prophecy hundreds of years earlier, nailing the timing of His Son's arrival and sacrifice.

# from 16018, 17032, 2299, 9126
--- The stone and the sign of Jonas
kicker: Christ foretold
big: Daniel 2:34-35 | mark: a stone was cut out without hands
p: The cornerstone laid before the foundation ([[Job 38:6]]). The stone cut out without hands that becomes a great mountain and fills the whole earth.
p: Three days and nights in the heart of the earth ([[Matthew 12:40]]). The timing is a minor doctrine, and yet its corruption leads to heresy: that Jesus didn't suffer in Hell as a burnt offering for sin, or not for 3 days and nights as the Bible says. *This day is this scripture fulfilled in your ears* ([[Luke 4:21]]).
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~6501 | Coats of skins: the first promise of Christ
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~7116 | God will provide Himself a lamb
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~17753 | Psalm 22 and the sufferings of the cross
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~16055 | The seventy weeks point to Jesus

=== Old Testament pictures of Christ
# from 6976, 7344, 10370
--- The LORD appeared
kicker: Pictures of Christ
big: Genesis 18:1 | mark: And the LORD appeared unto him
p: This is an Old Testament manifestation of Christ Jesus, appearing with two angels before Abraham on their way to judge Sodom. *No man hath seen God at any time, the only begotten Son... he hath declared him* ([[John 1:18]]).
p: Jacob wrestled with a man until the breaking of the day ([[Genesis 32:30]]). The angel sent before Moses was Christ, God with us: *My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest* ([[Exodus 33:14]]).

# from 12636, 12619, 10149
--- The serpent, the rock, the bread
kicker: Pictures of Christ
big: John 3:14 | mark: as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of man be lifted up
p: “If God be real, why bad stuff happen?” They are spoiled by their own lack of faith and gratitude. And God gives them the brazen serpent, lifted up, that whoever looked upon it lived ([[Numbers 21:8-9]]).
p: The rock smitten once, then only to be spoken to ([[Numbers 20:8-12]]; [[1 Corinthians 10:4]]). Manna, the bread which came down from heaven ([[John 6:32-35]]). Like the entire story of Exodus, a picture of salvation in Christ.

# from 7462, 16058, 12154
--- Joseph and his brethren
kicker: Pictures of Christ
big: Genesis 37:8 | mark: And they hated him yet the more for his dreams
p: They hate the favoritism Jacob gives Joseph, and that he's tattled on their sin. In parallel to Christ we see the resentment. Like the Jews' resentment of Christians, the older hating the younger because of the prophecy of who will reign.
p: Daniel saw a glorified Jesus by the river, eyes as lamps of fire, arms and feet as polished brass ([[Daniel 10:5-6]]; [[Revelation 1:13-15]]). Not Gabriel: Daniel had already met that angel.
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~6976 | The Judge of all the earth at Abraham's tent
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~12636 | The brazen serpent lifted up
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~7462 | Joseph's Brothers Hated Him as the Jews Hated Christ

=== The tabernacle and the sacrifices
# from 10263, 10270, 15014
--- A pattern of heavenly things
kicker: The tabernacle
big: Hebrews 8:5 | mark: Who serve unto the example and shadow of heavenly things
p: Everything in the tabernacle is a picture of Christ. It may seem like an Ikea assembly manual, and in the view of modern theologies that strip Christ from the “Jewish Bible,” the Old Testament becomes meaningless. But every aspect matters. Blue, purple and scarlet: the colors of the bruises and blood of Christ ([[Exodus 26:1]]).
p: Why did Christ die in this manner? Man by our nature knows sin requires a sacrifice for atonement. Every animal sacrificed, from Adam and Eve to Abel to Noah to Moses, were pictures of the actual sacrifice to come.

# from 11048, 11049, 11076, 11344
--- The burnt offering and the scapegoat
kicker: The tabernacle
big: Leviticus 1:3-4 | mark: of his own voluntary will; it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him
p: The burnt offering is both of a man's own free will, and is an offering for substitutionary atonement. Not a man chosen before time by God. Not some elect men, drawn and compelled. But by his own voluntary will.
p: The sin offering a picture of Jesus; the scapegoat a picture of the remission of sin, *all their transgressions in all their sins*, carried away into the wilderness to be remembered no more ([[Leviticus 16:21-22]]).

# from 12601, 7117, 2266, 11251, 9168, 13636
--- Cedar, scarlet and hyssop
kicker: The tabernacle
big: Leviticus 14:4 | mark: two birds alive and clean, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop
p: We see the wood of the cross, the scarlet of the blood, and the hyssop, the same used by the Roman guard to give Jesus the vinegar to drink ([[John 19:29]]). Leprosy is a picture of sin, and its miraculous healing, of the saving grace of God.
p: The red heifer without blemish, slain and burned without the camp with cedar, hyssop and scarlet, is an explicit picture of Christ ([[Numbers 19:2-6]]; [[Hebrews 13:12]]). The burnt offerings were all a picture of Christ Jesus. Not a prophecy of the Jews today.

# from 12399, 12401, 12404, 12405
--- The camp laid out as a cross
kicker: The tabernacle
big: Numbers 24:5 | mark: How goodly are thy tents, O Jacob
p: The camps surround the Tabernacle, the throne of God: Judah to the East, larger than the others; West a bit smaller; North and South almost equal ([[Numbers 2:2-3]]). While we cannot know with 100% certainty that the layout was a cross, it certainly is what is described, in my opinion.
p: Balaam looked down on the camp and marveled. Four standards, as the four faces of the cherubim about the throne of God: a lion, an ox, a man and an eagle ([[Ezekiel 1:10]]). Nothing in the Bible is incidental, accidental or coincidental.

# from 17816, 17835, 13712, 12562
--- He sat down
kicker: The tabernacle
big: Hebrews 10:11-12 | mark: sat down on the right hand of God
p: In the Tabernacle there were no chairs. A priest could never sit down because his job was never done. But Jesus, the author and finisher of our faith, sat down. Not a bone of Him broken, the Passover lamb ([[Psalms 34:20]]; [[John 19:36]]).
p: Not a cracker. Not a wafer. The blood of Christ was shed on that hill in Jerusalem; it isn't in a cup of juice or wine. Ordinances are a memorial. They themselves have no power ([[1 Corinthians 11:24-26]]).
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~10263 | The tabernacle, a pattern of heavenly things
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~11049 | The burnt offering: free will and substitution
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~12399 | The camp of Israel laid out as a cross
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~17816 | The priests stood, but Christ sat down

=== The feasts fulfilled in Christ
# from 13747, 11478, 2265, 9753
--- Christ our passover
kicker: The feasts fulfilled
big: 1 Corinthians 5:7 | mark: For even Christ our passover is sacrificed for us
p: Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread, First Fruits, and the Feast of Weeks, Pentecost, were given as a picture of Christ's first coming. The Passover lamb, Christ's sacrifice. The purging of the leaven, the remission of sin. First Fruits, His resurrection.
p: The lamb without blemish brought before the people on the 10th day, slain on the 14th, the blood upon the wooden door posts ([[Exodus 12:3-7]]). Three days without work, as Jesus does it all. We can do nothing.

# from 7743, 2367, 13079
--- Pentecost and the fall feasts
kicker: The feasts fulfilled
big: Leviticus 23:24 | mark: a memorial of blowing of trumpets
p: Pentecost, the Feast of Harvest, the day the gospel was preached and the firstfruits gathered in ([[Acts 2:1]]). The spring feasts picture His first coming; the fall feasts, trumpets, atonement and tabernacles, His second.
p: On these sabbaths NO WORK was to be done. The reinforcement of His grace in giving us a free gift of salvation in Jesus, who is the Sabbath. Those who did any work were cut off ([[Leviticus 23:30]]). So too will it be in the second coming.
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~13747 | The feasts of the LORD, Passover and the word Easter
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~7743 | The Fall Feasts Picture the Second Coming

=== Christ our King and High Priest
# from 6814, 8615, 16525
--- After the order of Melchisedec
kicker: King and High Priest
big: Genesis 14:18 | mark: Melchizedek king of Salem brought forth bread and wine: and he was the priest of the most high God
p: Melchizedek is seen as an early appearance of Jesus, the king of peace, without beginning or end, *made like unto the Son of God; abideth a priest continually* ([[Hebrews 7:3]]).
p: Joshua the high priest crowned: *The BRANCH... shall be a priest upon his throne* ([[Zechariah 6:12-13]]). Both King and Priest. They who were under the law have no need of the human priests given by Moses.

# from 12581, 12602, 15136, 11341, 8552
--- Aaron's rod, the covenant of salt, the veil
kicker: King and High Priest
big: Hebrews 4:16 | mark: Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace
p: Aaron's rod, a dead branch brought to life, is a clear and obvious picture of Christ Jesus ([[Numbers 17:8]]). The covenant of salt is bestowed on a priesthood and a kingdom ([[Numbers 18:19]]; [[2 Chronicles 13:5]]). Both fulfilled in Christ Jesus.
p: The high priest entered behind the veil once a year. But when Christ died, that veil was torn ([[Matthew 27:51]]). There is no calling on a “saint,” or “Mary” to intercede. There is only faith in God's word and His perfect work.

# from 14225, 17645, 14032
--- Mephibosheth at the king's table
kicker: King and High Priest
big: 2 Samuel 9:13 | mark: he did eat continually at the king’s table
p: Mephibosheth is a picture of a sinner, seeking grace in the eyes of the King. He was crippled in youth, as we are in sin. Custom would have the heirs of the previous king killed, yet David pardons him and sets him up as an adopted son, welcome at his table forever.
p: *Why do the heathen rage?* ([[Psalms 2:1-2]]) Kings and rulers, presidents and popes, all seek to be freed from the ways of the Lord. *Kiss the Son, lest he be angry* ([[Psalms 2:12]]).
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~6814 | Melchizedek, a picture of Christ
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~12581 | Aaron's rod that budded
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~14225 | Mephibosheth at the king's table

=== Christ and His bride
# from 13868, 13879
--- The kinsman redeemer
kicker: Christ and His bride
big: Ruth 3:9 | mark: spread therefore thy skirt over thine handmaid; for thou art a near kinsman
p: The nearer kinsman could redeem the land, but not Ruth, to raise the name of the dead. This is a picture of the Law itself. By the Law the people could keep their inheritance, but the Law is unable to redeem the person, and raise their name from the dead. The law could not redeem. Boaz could ([[Ruth 4:6-10]]).

# from 15279, 15276, 16791
--- Hosea buys back the adulteress
kicker: Christ and His bride
big: Hosea 2:16 | mark: thou shalt call me Ishi; and shalt call me no more Baali
p: The Lord instructed the prophet to love a woman who is an adulteress, just as Israel played the harlot to their God. The people wickedly left His protection for wine and idols, as an unfaithful wife ([[Hosea 3:1-2]]).
p: And yet, from the wilderness, *the valley of Achor for a door of hope* ([[Hosea 2:15]]). Why one? *That he might seek a godly seed* ([[Malachi 2:15]]). The promise was always Christ.

# from 17562, 17565, 17570, 17579, 17581, 17588
--- Song of Solomon
kicker: Christ and His bride
big: Song of Solomon 2:10 | mark: Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away
p: The clear allegory of Christ and His beloved, the saved. He is the tree of life, over a precious flower among the thorns. She seeks him in the night, as at the empty tomb, and finds *him whom my soul loveth* ([[Song of Solomon 3:4]]).
p: Battered by the watchmen, she still sings his praise: *This is my beloved, and this is my friend* ([[Song of Solomon 5:16]]). Unsaved people who see Christians suffer for Christ and still preach His love are often baffled, but sometimes moved. *Set me as a seal upon thine heart* ([[Song of Solomon 8:6]]).

# from 17932, 17946, 15964
--- The King's daughter
kicker: Christ and His bride
big: Psalms 45:10-11 | mark: forget also thine own people, and thy father’s house
p: Psalm 45 is a doctrine-rich wedding song that speaks clearly of the Lord Jesus, a bride brought to Him. At His right hand stands the queen, decked in gold of Ophir. Her beauty provided by the King, to set apart the bride. The church.
p: *Thou shalt be called Hephzibah, and thy land Beulah* ([[Isaiah 62:4]]). The New Jerusalem coming down from Heaven, decked as a bride ([[Revelation 21:2]]).
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~13879 | The law could not redeem, Boaz could
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~15279 | Hosea buys back the adulteress
read: app:doctrine-christ-ot~17562 | I am black, but comely: Christ and His beloved

=== The scarlet thread
--- The Scarlet Thread [title]
overline: Christ in the Old Testament
heading: The Scarlet Thread
big: John 5:39 | mark: they are they which testify of me
center: Nothing in Scripture is incidental, accidental or coincidental. And ultimately, everything points to Jesus.
